

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# PHASE 2 DATA SAFETY
# Pipeline outputs contain RECORDS, not parameters: the tidy and
# labeled CSVs are the source data reshaped, and generated.csv is
# derived from a profile of it. When the source is real clinical
# data these must never leave the machine. Profiles and specs are
# aggregates by construction, but they still deserve a governance
# decision rather than a habit — so runs are ignored wholesale.
# The mimic set is exempt: it is synthetic and regenerable by seed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
data/phase2_run/
data/real*/
*_real*.csv
*_real*profile.json
tidy_visits*.csv
!data/mimic_omop/tidy_visits*.csv

# The rules above are PATH-ANCHORED, and placement defeated them: a
# --window run whose %USERPROFILE% failed to expand wrote 15 MB of
# real-derived output to a stray folder in the repo root, where none
# of data/phase2_run/ or data/real*/ matched it. A pipeline artifact
# is identified by its NAME, so ignore these wherever they land and
# exempt only the two synthetic fixtures that are meant to be tracked.
condnet_model.json
generated_*.csv
fidelity_*.json
profile.json
!data/mimic_omop/profile.json
!data/mimic_omop/fidelity.json
!docs/e2e/generated_patients.csv

# The discover/blueprint/generate path writes DIFFERENT names, and
# `generated_*.csv` does not match `generated.csv` - so every artifact
# of the new pipeline was committable. Verified before this line
# existed: blueprint.json, catalogue.json, findings.txt and
# generated.csv all staged cleanly from a repo-root run.
#
# All four are derived from whatever was read. generated.csv is
# synthetic but built from the source's shape; the blueprint holds
# k-anonymised quantiles and response curves; findings.txt names real
# columns and real values. Aggregates deserve a governance decision
# rather than a habit, which is what the rule above already says.
generated.csv
blueprint.json
catalogue.json
findings.txt
fidelity.json
!data/mimic_omop/generated.csv
!data/mimic_omop/fidelity.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# PRIVATE — PRESENTER NOTES
# docs/presenter_companion.html is a teleprompter: verbatim
# scripts, rehearsal notes, and answers written for one person to
# read while presenting. It is not documentation and was never
# meant for colleagues or for an enterprise mirror. Regenerate it
# locally with scripts/build_presenter.py when needed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
docs/presenter_companion.html
data/scratch_check/

# build and run artifacts — never tracked
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
build/
dist/

# generated output directories
tables/
campaigns/
corpora/
runs/
out/
gui_runs/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.env
.DS_Store
campaigns/
corpus/
corpora/


